From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: tag_vsc73xx_8021q: use the bridge VID when
 transmitting to a bridged port

Joining a bridge replaces a port's standalone tag_8021q VLAN with the
bridge's VLAN (dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_join() adds the bridge VID and
deletes the standalone one). The xmit path, however, only uses the
bridge VID when skb->offload_fwd_mark is set, and otherwise tags with
the standalone VID -- a VID the switch no longer has for that port, so
the frame is dropped.

That is not reachable while everything goes through the bridge, because
bridge-forwarded frames carry the mark. It is reachable as soon as
something transmits straight onto the user port instead: the netfilter
flowtable's direct transmit path does exactly this once
dev_fill_forward_path() has resolved a bridge port, and every packet of
such a flow is then lost.

Measured on an IPQ5332 board with an RTL8372N switch (rtl837x, which
reuses this tagger): with the flowtable forwarding through the bridge,
frames towards the client carry the bridge VID 3088 and arrive; with the
flowtable transmitting directly to the port, they carry the standalone
VID 3076 and the client receives nothing, while the switch's own FDB has
the client on a different port entirely.

Use the bridge VID whenever a port on a VLAN-unaware bridge is
transmitted to, not just for already-forwarded frames. The switch then
selects the egress port from its own FDB, which is what it does for
bridge-forwarded traffic anyway, and a frame can no longer be tagged
with a VLAN the port does not have.

VLAN-aware bridges are deliberately left exactly as they were. There
every frame carries one of the bridge's own VLANs and the switch
classifies by those, so tag_8021q does not decide the egress port and
the untagged-return path stays restricted to bridge-forwarded frames.

Bridge-forwarded traffic is unaffected: dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_join() sets
tx_fwd_offload, and the bridge already marks what it forwards or
originates, so that path took the bridge-VID branch before this change
too. What changes is only frames that bypass bridge forwarding and are
transmitted directly on a port of a VLAN-unaware bridge.

Link-local traffic (STP, LLDP, PTP, EAPOL) is addressed to one specific
link and must keep precise targeting, so it is carved out and still uses
the standalone VID, the way tag_sja1105.c carves link-local frames out
before its own imprecise path. For that to work the standalone VLAN has
to stay present in hardware while the port is bridged; the rtl837x
driver keeps it (the port's PVID is the bridge VLAN, so ingress
classification and isolation are unchanged).

Signed-off-by: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/dsa/tag_vsc73xx_8021q.c
+++ b/net/dsa/tag_vsc73xx_8021q.c
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 /* Copyright (C) 2024 Pawel Dembicki <paweldembicki@gmail.com>
  */
 #include <linux/dsa/8021q.h>
+#include <linux/etherdevice.h>
 
 #include "tag.h"
 #include "tag_8021q.h"
@@ -13,17 +14,43 @@
 {
 	struct dsa_port *dp = dsa_user_to_port(netdev);
 	u16 queue_mapping = skb_get_queue_mapping(skb);
+	unsigned int bridge_num = dsa_port_bridge_num_get(dp);
+	struct net_device *br = dsa_port_bridge_dev_get(dp);
 	u16 tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_standalone_vid(dp);
 	u8 pcp;
 
-	if (skb->offload_fwd_mark) {
-		unsigned int bridge_num = dsa_port_bridge_num_get(dp);
-		struct net_device *br = dsa_port_bridge_dev_get(dp);
-
-		if (br_vlan_enabled(br))
-			return skb;
-
-		tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(bridge_num);
+	/* Link-local traffic (STP, LLDP, PTP, EAPOL) is addressed to one
+	 * specific link, so it keeps the standalone VID and the precise
+	 * targeting that comes with it. The driver is expected to keep
+	 * that VLAN present in hardware for bridged ports.
+	 */
+	if (is_link_local_ether_addr(eth_hdr(skb)->h_dest))
+		br = NULL;
+
+	if (bridge_num && br) {
+		/* A VLAN-aware bridge tags every frame with one of its own
+		 * VLANs and the switch classifies by those, so tag_8021q has
+		 * no say in where the frame goes. Leave that case exactly as
+		 * it was: only what the bridge itself forwarded goes out
+		 * without a tag_8021q header.
+		 */
+		if (br_vlan_enabled(br)) {
+			if (skb->offload_fwd_mark)
+				return skb;
+		} else {
+			/* A bridged port has no standalone VLAN in hardware:
+			 * joining a bridge replaces it with the bridge's VLAN.
+			 * Sending with the standalone VID would hand the switch
+			 * a VID it does not have and the frame is dropped --
+			 * which happens for anything transmitted straight onto
+			 * the port instead of through the bridge, such as the
+			 * netfilter flowtable's direct transmit path. Use the
+			 * bridge VID for those too and let the switch pick the
+			 * egress port from its own FDB, exactly as it does for
+			 * bridge-forwarded frames.
+			 */
+			tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(bridge_num);
+		}
 	}
 
 	pcp = netdev_txq_to_tc(netdev, queue_mapping);
